            "Internal Setup (IED - Inside Exchange of Die) encompasses all changeover operations that can only be performed while the machine is completely stopped and powered down. Physically unbolting a heavy die from the press bed, dismounting a milling cutter spindle, or sanitizing a food processing vessel are true internal setup tasks. External Setup (OED - Outside Exchange of Die) encompasses all setup operations that can be performed while the machine is still actively running and producing good parts from the previous production run. Locating the next die in the warehouse, pre-heating plastic injection molds, staging raw material pallets, pre-setting cutting tool offsets on an optical presetter, and retrieving torque wrenches are all external setup tasks.",
